---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SUPPORT_EMAIL, PHONE_DISPLAY, mailtoHref, telHref } from '@/lib/contact';

const title = 'Privacy Policy';
const description =
  'How NutaSolutions collects, uses, and protects personal information for NutaPOS and related websites under Ghana data protection law.';
const lastUpdated = 'September 10, 2026';
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonicalPath="/privacy">
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 pb-24 pt-32 md:px-6 md:pt-36">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-medium tracking-tight text-surface-900">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-muted">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
    <div class="mt-10 max-w-none space-y-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
      <p>
        This Privacy Policy explains how NutaSolutions (“NutaSolutions,” “we,” “us,” or “our”) collects, uses, stores,
        shares, and protects personal information when you visit our websites, create an account, or use NutaPOS and
        related services (together, the “Services”).
      </p>
      <p>
        We process personal data in line with the Data Protection Act, 2012 (Act 843) of Ghana and other applicable
        laws. By using the Services, you acknowledge the practices described here.
      </p>

      <h2 class="!mt-10 text-2xl font-medium tracking-tight text-surface-900">1. Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        NutaSolutions provides NutaPOS, a cloud point-of-sale and business management platform for inventory, sales,
        bookkeeping, staff access, audits, and related operations, primarily for businesses in Ghana and across Africa.
        Related sites (including NutaWEB roadmap pages) are covered by this policy unless a separate notice says
        otherwise.
      </p>
      <p>
        Privacy requests and questions: email
        <a href={mailtoHref('Privacy request')} class="text-brand-600 hover:text-brand-700">{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a>
        or call
        <a href={telHref()} class="text-brand-600 hover:text-brand-700">{PHONE_DISPLAY}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2 class="!mt-10 text-2xl font-medium tracking-tight text-surface-900">2. Scope</h2>
      <p>This policy applies to:</p>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">
        <li>Visitors to our marketing and product websites</li>
        <li>People who sign up, sign in, or request sales information</li>
        <li>Authorized users of a customer’s NutaPOS account (owners, managers, and staff)</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        It does not replace privacy notices that our merchant customers must give to their own end customers or
        employees when they use NutaPOS in their stores.
      </p>

      <h2 class="!mt-10 text-2xl font-medium tracking-tight text-surface-900">3. Roles: controller and processor</h2>
      <p>
        <strong class="font-medium text-surface-900">Account and site data.</strong> For information you provide to
        create an account, contact sales, or browse our sites (such as your name, email, phone, and business profile),
        NutaSolutions is typically the data controller: we decide why and how that data is processed.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong class="font-medium text-surface-900">Customer Content.</strong> Data that customers and their staff enter
        into NutaPOS—such as sales and receipts, inventory and stock movements, bookkeeping records, staff profiles and
        roles, audit logs, and any end-customer details captured at checkout—is “Customer Content.” For Customer
        Content, the merchant customer is the data controller. NutaSolutions acts as a data processor: we process that
        data on the customer’s instructions to provide the Services.
      </p>

      <h2 class="!mt-10 text-2xl font-medium tracking-tight text-surface-900">4. Information we collect</h2>
      <h3 class="!mt-6 text-xl font-medium tracking-tight text-surface-900">4.1 Information you provide</h3>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">
        <li>
          <strong class="font-medium text-surface-900">Account signup:</strong> full name, email address, password,
          phone number, business name, business type, business location, number of branches, and how you heard about
          us.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="font-medium text-surface-900">Sign-in:</strong> email and password (and related authentication
          tokens managed by our systems).
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="font-medium text-surface-900">Communications:</strong> messages you send by email, phone, or
          other channels, including sales inquiries.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <h3 class="!mt-6 text-xl font-medium tracking-tight text-surface-900">4.2 Customer Content</h3>
      <p>
        When you use NutaPOS, we process the business and operational data you and your team upload or generate in the
        product, including transaction, inventory, staff, and bookkeeping data as configured for your account.
      </p>
      <h3 class="!mt-6 text-xl font-medium tracking-tight text-surface-900">4.3 Technical and usage data</h3>
      <p>
        We may collect limited technical information needed to operate and secure the Services, such as IP address,
        device/browser type, timestamps, and diagnostic or security logs related to authentication and API use.
      </p>
      <h3 class="!mt-6 text-xl font-medium tracking-tight text-surface-900">4.4 What we do not do</h3>
      <p>
        We do not sell personal data. Our marketing website does not currently use third-party advertising or analytics
        cookies. If that changes, we will update this policy.
      </p>

      <h2 class="!mt-10 text-2xl font-medium tracking-tight text-surface-900">5. Purposes of processing</h2>
      <p>We use personal information to:</p>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">
        <li>Create and manage accounts, authenticate users, and provide NutaPOS</li>
        <li>Host and process Customer Content on behalf of our customers</li>
        <li>Respond to support and sales requests</li>
        <li>Secure the Services, prevent abuse, and troubleshoot incidents</li>
        <li>Improve product reliability and features (using aggregated or de-identified insights where practical)</li>
        <li>Send service-related notices (for example, security or account messages)</li>
        <li>Comply with law, enforce our Terms of Service, and protect our rights</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We apply Act 843 principles including lawful processing, purpose limitation, data minimisation, accuracy,
        storage limitation, and integrity and confidentiality.
      </p>

      <h2 class="!mt-10 text-2xl font-medium tracking-tight text-surface-900">6. Cookies and similar technologies</h2>
      <p>
        Our marketing site is primarily static and does not rely on advertising trackers. The application and API may
        use essential cookies or local storage for sessions, authentication, and security. You can control cookies
        through your browser; blocking essential cookies may prevent sign-in or core features from working.
      </p>

      <h2 class="!mt-10 text-2xl font-medium tracking-tight text-surface-900">7. How we share information</h2>
      <p>We may share personal information with:</p>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">
        <li>
          <strong class="font-medium text-surface-900">Service providers / subprocessors</strong> who host
          infrastructure, email, or other operational services under contractual confidentiality and security
          obligations
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="font-medium text-surface-900">Professional advisers</strong> (legal, accounting) where needed
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="font-medium text-surface-900">Authorities</strong> when required by law or to protect rights,
          safety, or security
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="font-medium text-surface-900">Business transfers</strong> in connection with a merger,
          acquisition, or restructuring, subject to appropriate safeguards
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Customer Content is accessible to the customer’s authorized users according to roles configured in NutaPOS. We
        do not disclose Customer Content to unrelated third parties except as needed to provide the Services or as
        required by law.
      </p>

      <h2 class="!mt-10 text-2xl font-medium tracking-tight text-surface-900">8. International transfers</h2>
      <p>
        The Services use cloud infrastructure. Personal data and Customer Content may be stored or processed on servers
        located outside Ghana. Where we transfer personal data internationally, we take steps consistent with Act 843
        to protect it, including contractual and technical safeguards with our providers.
      </p>

      <h2 class="!mt-10 text-2xl font-medium tracking-tight text-surface-900">9. Retention</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">
        <li>
          <strong class="font-medium text-surface-900">Account and contact data:</strong> kept while your account is
          active and for a reasonable period afterward for security, dispute resolution, and legal compliance.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="font-medium text-surface-900">Customer Content:</strong> retained for the life of the
          subscription and deleted or returned according to our Terms and the customer’s instructions, subject to
          backup and legal hold cycles.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="font-medium text-surface-900">Logs:</strong> typically retained for shorter operational periods
          unless needed longer for security or legal reasons.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="!mt-10 text-2xl font-medium tracking-tight text-surface-900">10. Security</h2>
      <p>
        We implement appropriate technical and organisational measures to protect personal data against unauthorised
        access, loss, or misuse. These include encryption-minded architecture, access controls, role-based permissions
        in NutaPOS, and resilient hosting practices. No method of transmission or storage is completely secure; we work
        continuously to reduce risk. Where a security compromise involving personal data occurs, we will take steps
        consistent with applicable law, including notifying affected controllers and, where required, the Data
        Protection Commission.
      </p>

      <h2 class="!mt-10 text-2xl font-medium tracking-tight text-surface-900">11. Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Subject to Act 843 and other applicable law, individuals may have rights to access personal data we hold about
        them, request correction of inaccurate data, object to certain processing, and request deletion or restriction
        where appropriate. To exercise these rights for data we control, contact
        <a href={mailtoHref('Privacy request')} class="text-brand-600 hover:text-brand-700">{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        For Customer Content processed on behalf of a merchant, please contact that merchant first; we will assist
        customers in responding to valid requests as required.
      </p>
      <p>
        You may also lodge a complaint with the Data Protection Commission of Ghana if you believe your rights have
        been infringed.
      </p>

      <h2 class="!mt-10 text-2xl font-medium tracking-tight text-surface-900">12. Children</h2>
      <p>
        The Services are designed for businesses and adult users. They are not directed at children, and we do not
        knowingly collect personal data from children for marketing or account creation.
      </p>

      <h2 class="!mt-10 text-2xl font-medium tracking-tight text-surface-900">13. Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. The “Last updated” date at the top will change when we do.
        For material changes, we may provide additional notice (for example, by email or in-product message). Continued
        use of the Services after an update constitutes acceptance of the revised policy where permitted by law.
      </p>

      <h2 class="!mt-10 text-2xl font-medium tracking-tight text-surface-900">14. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        NutaSolutions<br />
        Email:
        <a href={mailtoHref('Privacy request')} class="text-brand-600 hover:text-brand-700">{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a><br />
        Phone:
        <a href={telHref()} class="text-brand-600 hover:text-brand-700">{PHONE_DISPLAY}</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
